{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing","id":1399018,"title":"Is mutual Blood Bonding between Kindred couples a good thing or a bad thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-26T04:43:18-07:00","id":1399018,"title":"Is mutual Blood Bonding between Kindred couples a good thing or a bad thing?","content":"What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> Also, can the Wan Gui create or enter into Blood Bonds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T04:56:32-07:00","id":1399022,"title":"","content":"kuei jin have their own version of vinculum<br /> <br /> and most couples who don't mutally bond are not sustainable<br /> <br /> kuei-jin don't need to mutually bond, since with Yang imbalance, they can live like mortals,<br /> they don't have to suffer the same insecurities that cainites do","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T06:03:47-07:00","id":1399042,"title":"","content":"It is said that the mutual blood bond is in most cases like a marriage vow to make two vampires keep any feeling to each other but some are reluctant to do it because it can happen that after centuries your love will turn into hate so it will end up like Mr. and Mrs. Smith but without good ending.<br /> <br /> From my opinion it is a good thing because it keeps you to a person you have good feeling and ensure you some sort of trust because it is like Maoyuu Maou Yuusha where a marriage is giving the other person each other your own right. Another positiv effect is, that you can not without nothing blood bound to another vampire and so the best is you will have maximal the effect of a vinculum lvl 5 on you from an unwanted person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 06-26-2020, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T07:43:34-07:00","id":1399062,"title":"","content":"Thank you both. That\u2019s very helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T09:09:58-07:00","id":1399081,"title":"","content":"I thought I saw in one of the old books it was mentioned that over time as their true love fades and is only held in place by the blood bond, it becomes a pale artificial imitation of the real thing. Eventually one or both of them might just get sick of it over the centuries. I have no clue where this came from, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T09:14:14-07:00","id":1399082,"title":"","content":"Its fine if you actually love each other. If ever you fall out of love, it's like Lilith and Desus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T10:13:08-07:00","id":1399095,"title":"","content":"This dips a bit into Requiem discussion a bit I think, but they have a term for this in 2nd Ed: &quot;the Perversion.&quot; (<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Perversion\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Perversion</a>)<br /> <br /> As noted above, such a situation can work pretty well for the Kindred involved in the relationship, as long as their artificially-enforced relationship doesn't turn sour. But the reason it gets such a bad rap in VtR has to do with the effect it has on the couple's relationship with the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> Remember, a blood-bond is not supposed to be depicted as a 'healthy' love or attachment. It's more akin to the sort of brainwashing we associate with &quot;love potions,&quot; and often tend towards obsessive. Now, take two vampires, with a hunger for blood they constantly need to satisfy, and a Beast that can go off the handle over all sorts of things. Then make those two vampires OBSESSED with each other. Taking care of each other is now the most important thing in both of their unlives. And they are now immune to blood-bonds to other Kindred.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of a ticking time-bomb for a &quot;Bonnie and Clyde&quot; situation, or a psychotic rampage of revenge if one of the lovers gets killed off in the inevitable conflicts of vampire existence. Along with the risk of them developing an addiction to vitae or diablerie and then protecting one another as they go off the edge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 06-26-2020, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T11:41:15-07:00","id":1399105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399081#post1399081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought I saw in one of the old books it was mentioned that over time as their true love fades and is only held in place by the blood bond, it becomes a pale artificial imitation of the real thing. Eventually one or both of them might just get sick of it over the centuries. I have no clue where this came from, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It whas only normal love, not true love. True love is so rare that some think it is a (possible) requirement for Golconda. True Love is something that overcomes the ages though I think it whas said, that it is something only between two people. So having two sisters/friends etc falling in love with the same guy and the guy cares for both then it is only ordinary but not TRUE love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T11:55:20-07:00","id":1399107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399105#post1399105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It whas only normal love, not true love. True love is so rare that some think it is a (possible) requirement for Golconda. True Love is something that overcomes the ages though I think it whas said, that it is something only between two people. So having two sisters/friends etc falling in love with the same guy and the guy cares for both then it is only ordinary but not TRUE love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure about that. I guess if you're talking fairy tale level true love happily ever after, it might, but that level of affection would be extremely hard to maintain when you have eternity stretching out before you and a beast inside. Like I said before, though, this is something I vaguely remember and can't recall where the hell I read it, so I could be off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T11:59:16-07:00","id":1399111,"title":"","content":"True Love is so amazing that it can allow a farm boy to beat a fencing wizard in a duel, out-wrestle a giant, and defeat a man who makes Plato, Aristotle, and Socrates seem like morons in a battle of wits.<br /> <br /> But what about a mutual blood bond? The problem with the blood bond is that it is a magically imposed obsessive love, not actual love. Real love between people is based on qualities of those people, how they interact with each other, in shared values and experiences, on elevating each other. The blood bond doesn\u2019t need those things, so the obsessive feelings of love could continue even if the person who shares your mutual obsession makes you miserable, even if you grow apart and are destructive towards each other - the unnatural love persists. That sounds very dangerous to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T12:07:16-07:00","id":1399112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing#post1399018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> Also, can the Wan Gui create or enter into Blood Bonds?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The blood bond does generate a form of artificial love akin to psychological slavery and causes very real addiction (especially in mortals who after a while need the blood like it was a drug and need it to stay alive after a few decades). So no, it's not a good thing at all. The feelings a mutual blood makes surface are usually extreme jealousy and possessive tendencies, it can also cause sudden mood swings even in older vampires. The lover becomes a thing to be possessed. Freedom, an already difficult concept for vampires, becomes a menace to be stomped out. Cruelty and obsessions usually surface and make vampires who enact mutual blood bonds loathe each other not long after the third sip is drunk.<br /> <br /> 2. I never cared one bit about the Cathayans so I cannot answer that though being restless dead being given flesh again and not being centered as much as Western vamps on blood I suppose they could not have been given the means to blood bond one another and mortals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T12:11:28-07:00","id":1399113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399111#post1399111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what about a mutual blood bond? The problem with the blood bond is that it is a magically imposed obsessive love, not actual love. Real love between people is based on qualities of those people, how they interact with each other, in shared values and experiences, on elevating each other. The blood bond doesn\u2019t need those things, so the obsessive feelings of love could continue even if the person who shares your mutual obsession makes you miserable, even if you grow apart and are destructive towards each other - the unnatural love persists. That sounds very dangerous to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The blood bond's love is all the things you just described and more. It's based on the qualities of those people (having the blood) in shared values and experiences (giving blood) and on elevating eachother (A person with blood this good must be great)<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, the blood bond is superior to &quot;actual love&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T12:41:04-07:00","id":1399120,"title":"","content":"Presumably, a pair of Kindred don't enter into a mutual Blood Bond unless they have some kind of chemistry. If they didn't, they wouldn't willingly drink each other's vitae. (And if one did it secretly to the other, they have no reason to make it mutual unless they already love that Kindred).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T12:41:10-07:00","id":1399121,"title":"","content":"The bond replicated the feelings of being <i>in </i>love, which, let\u2019s be honest, is kind of like being drugged by your hormones even in normal circumstances. But whereas that feeling normally fades over time, the blood bond can be maintained indefinitely. <br /> <br /> What the blood bond can\u2019t synthesize is the more dispassionate respect and care that we associate with long-term love, which is more of a choice than an emotion. Vampiric couples may have that or not, but it\u2019s got little to do with blood play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T12:48:10-07:00","id":1399124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399121#post1399121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bond replicated the feelings of being <i>in </i>love, which, let\u2019s be honest, is kind of like being drugged by your hormones even in normal circumstances. But whereas that feeling normally fades over time, the blood bond can be maintained indefinitely.<br /> <br /> What the blood bond can\u2019t synthesize is the more dispassionate respect and care that we associate with long-term love, which is more of a choice than an emotion. Vampiric couples may have that or not, but it\u2019s got little to do with blood play.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good point. There is a difference between being in love with someone, and <i>loving</i> someone. The former is an emotion, the latter a continuous, deliberate action. The kind of mutual respect and concern for the feelings and wellbeing of the other are integral to real love, and may not be reflected in the Blood Bond. At the very least, there's no guarantee of it among immortal narcissists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T13:24:40-07:00","id":1399128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399111#post1399111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Love is so amazing that it can allow a farm boy to beat a fencing wizard in a duel, out-wrestle a giant, and defeat a man who makes Plato, Aristotle, and Socrates seem like morons in a battle of wits.<br /> <br /> But what about a mutual blood bond? The problem with the blood bond is that it is a magically imposed obsessive love, not actual love. Real love between people is based on qualities of those people, how they interact with each other, in shared values and experiences, on elevating each other. The blood bond doesn\u2019t need those things, so the obsessive feelings of love could continue even if the person who shares your mutual obsession makes you miserable, even if you grow apart and are destructive towards each other - the unnatural love persists. That sounds very dangerous to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew this was going to come up.<br /> <br /> It's also capable of making someone survive the horrors of war, getting raped by Bulgars, being married off to a governor to insure their financial well being, survive being hunted by the inquisition, leave behind an advanced society where the buildings are made of gold, enslavement by the Turks just to finally be reunited and find the girl's looks are gone, then settle on a farm only to find that they've all been changed so much by what they've seen and endured to find the life dull and quarellsome.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/19942-h/19942-h.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/images/001_th.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/19942-h/19942-h.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> The Project Gutenberg eBook of Candide, by Voltaire. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/19942-h/19942-h.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/19942-h/19942-h.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For every Buttercup and Wesley, there's probably a few Candides and Cun\u00e9gondes.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that true love between Vampires is impossible, just that it would be insanely hard to maintain. How many of the few that had it would even seek Golconda? How many are totally into the predator thing and would never even seek Golconda? How many of those that do seek it would even manage to find a tutor. How many wouldn't get in a situation where they sacrifice themselves for their lover? Making true love last for centuries as an undead predator should be insanely difficult. Not technically impossible, but so challenging that it's pretty much a legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T13:32:39-07:00","id":1399129,"title":"","content":"My own personal thought on this is that ultimately the Blood Bond can't help but be destructive -- primarily because it ACTIVELY interferes with the ability to have genuine emotions.<br /> <br /> Your lover asks you to do something for him or her -- to make some deep sacrifice. You know you want to do it... but you wonder, is it really what you want? Or is it just the bond? Your lover asks forgiveness for a serious trespass. You forgive him or her, but was it really because you loved him or her? <br /> <br /> Once you subject yourself to the bond, you can't trust that your own feelings are genuine. And if you can't trust them, you can't really say that you're feeling them. <br /> <br /> After even a few *decades* of this (let alone centuries) it would be enough to destroy any relationship.<br /> <br /> Except that you can't leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T14:10:14-07:00","id":1399135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399107#post1399107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not entirely sure about that. I guess if you're talking fairy tale level true love happily ever after, it might, but that level of affection would be extremely hard to maintain when you have eternity stretching out before you and a beast inside. Like I said before, though, this is something I vaguely remember and can't recall where the hell I read it, so I could be off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree it is rare. Not without reason it is said that it can be a way to reach Golconda because it is so fucking rare even more in the World of Darkness. And I remembered reading it in the V20 rulebook.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399113#post1399113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The blood bond's love is all the things you just described and more. It's based on the qualities of those people (having the blood) in shared values and experiences (giving blood) and on elevating eachother (A person with blood this good must be great)<br /> <br /> For all intents and purposes, the blood bond is superior to &quot;actual love&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Except True Love. Because True Love (with the help of very high Willpower) can help you break yourself a blood bond because this artificial created love which can be easily misused is nothing against the True Love.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399124#post1399124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very good point. There is a difference between being in love with someone, and <i>loving</i> someone. The former is an emotion, the latter a continuous, deliberate action. The kind of mutual respect and concern for the feelings and wellbeing of the other are integral to real love, and may not be reflected in the Blood Bond. At the very least, there's no guarantee of it among immortal narcissists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this together what you said before, can let it help you to keep genuine love with a partner blood bound to keep alive.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399128#post1399128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I knew this was going to come up.<br /> <br /> It's also capable of making someone survive the horrors of war, getting raped by Bulgars, being married off to a governor to insure their financial well being, survive being hunted by the inquisition, leave behind an advanced society where the buildings are made of gold, enslavement by the Turks just to finally be reunited and find the girl's looks are gone, then settle on a farm only to find that they've all been changed so much by what they've seen and endured to find the life dull and quarellsome.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/19942-h/19942-h.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/images/001_th.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/19942-h/19942-h.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> The Project Gutenberg eBook of Candide, by Voltaire. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/19942-h/19942-h.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.gutenberg.org/files/19942/19942-h/19942-h.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For every Buttercup and Wesley, there's probably a few Candides and Cun\u00e9gondes.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that true love between Vampires is impossible, just that it would be insanely hard to maintain. How many of the few that had it would even seek Golconda? How many are totally into the predator thing and would never even seek Golconda? How many of those that do seek it would even manage to find a tutor. How many wouldn't get in a situation where they sacrifice themselves for their lover? Making true love last for centuries as an undead predator should be insanely difficult. Not technically impossible, but so challenging that it's pretty much a legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of disagree. True Love is the love you get with the one person of all the ages from the whole earth. It is as you said following through all the hardships until the end of the earth because you only need to be there. The only thing from my opinion that can end this love is one lover is dying or you let her fail to experience the love because you understand that, she will never get to love one as much as yourself but you want rather have herself a mundane live in security then bring her to your dangerous live.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399129#post1399129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own personal thought on this is that ultimately the Blood Bond can't help but be destructive -- primarily because it ACTIVELY interferes with the ability to have genuine emotions.<br /> <br /> Your lover asks you to do something for him or her -- to make some deep sacrifice. You know you want to do it... but you wonder, is it really what you want? Or is it just the bond? Your lover asks forgiveness for a serious trespass. You forgive him or her, but was it really because you loved him or her?<br /> <br /> Once you subject yourself to the bond, you can't trust that your own feelings are genuine. And if you can't trust them, you can't really say that you're feeling them.<br /> <br /> After even a few *decades* of this (let alone centuries) it would be enough to destroy any relationship.<br /> <br /> Except that you can't leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that whas said too. Some vampires keep themselves from doing that (and mostly just keep themselves from experiencing any love too) because they can not be sure they will still feel that in a few centuries or because of it they will start to hate whom they loved before. From my opinion it can be both and is up to each round because it can be either, that this mutual bonding keep both in love because their nature hinders them to feel something elseway or it is destructing because they have the continously louder getting voice in their head, that your love will screw you over like someone that whas hurt very much before from someone that only played their love to him and so you can not bring yourself to really trust her that it is true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T14:26:29-07:00","id":1399137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399135#post1399135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of disagree. True Love is the love you get with the one person of all the ages from the whole earth. It is as you said following through all the hardships until the end of the earth because you only need to be there. The only thing from my opinion that can end this love is one lover is dying or you let her fail to experience the love because you understand that, she will never get to love one as much as yourself but you want rather have herself a mundane live in security then bring her to your dangerous live.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this comes down to how cynical you are (In my case very) and how tragic you want the WOD to be. My point was just in a single lifetime Candide and Cun\u00e9gonde had changed so much over the course of it, that they were no longer the people that had that bond of true love. Stretch that out over even more time and it'll tax even the strongest relationships. Once again, not saying it's impossible, but would be so difficult it'd be practically a myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T15:38:36-07:00","id":1399146,"title":"","content":"I feel strongly that the idea that the bloodbond isn't &quot;real love&quot; to be wishful thinking. IDK, maybe I've never experienced true love because I've seen some depictions in media and, though I've looked at people and genuinely felt happy that they were happy, happy to be with them, and absolutely sure that I'd be very upset if something happened to them, and retroactively I thought my IQ dropped a hundred points, <i>My vision never went pink and flowers did not materialise in my vision. </i> <br /> <br /> If the bloodbond does that to you, why isn't it love? I think you're looking at it from an ethical point of view, not a realistic point of view. <br /> <br /> Werewolves have a &quot;You absolutely want to fuck me power&quot; innate to them, and originally it only cared about target willpower and your good looks, but later on it got the caveat of &quot;but this power absolutely respects sexual orientation and doesn't work on people who don't like you&quot; and again, this is someone concerned about &quot;ethics&quot; rather than whats realistic (within a fantasy setting, yeah, nah, don't start that argument) <br /> <br /> Love is love, magical or hormonal or both. Saying &quot;blood bond is not real love&quot; is purely a matter of putting up an ethical shield around a scary topic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T15:41:44-07:00","id":1399148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399082#post1399082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its fine if you actually love each other. If ever you fall out of love, it's like Lilith and Desus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so you know, Desus got retconned out of 3e. Lillith's Solar mate in 3e was named Andamani.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T15:44:08-07:00","id":1399150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399082#post1399082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its fine if you actually love each other. If ever you fall out of love, it's like Lilith and Desus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s scary. For real.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a> what if one friend has over time developed something close to True Love for the guy and he definitely has feelings of True Love for her, but the other friend just really likes him?<br /> <br /> Of course, that\u2019s far afield from a mutual Blood Bond scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T15:51:27-07:00","id":1399151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399146#post1399146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel strongly that the idea that the bloodbond isn't &amp;quot;real love&amp;quot; to be wishful thinking. IDK, maybe I've never experienced true love because I've seen some depictions in media and, though I've looked at people and genuinely felt happy that they were happy, happy to be with them, and absolutely sure that I'd be very upset if something happened to them, and retroactively I thought my IQ dropped a hundred points, <i>My vision never went pink and flowers did not materialise in my vision. </i> <br /> <br /> If the bloodbond does that to you, why isn't it love? I think you're looking at it from an ethical point of view, not a realistic point of view. <br /> <br /> Werewolves have a &amp;quot;You absolutely want to fuck me power&amp;quot; innate to them, and originally it only cared about target willpower and your good looks, but later on it got the caveat of &amp;quot;but this power absolutely respects sexual orientation and doesn't work on people who don't like you&amp;quot; and again, this is someone concerned about &amp;quot;ethics&amp;quot; rather than whats realistic (within a fantasy setting, yeah, nah, don't start that argument) <br /> <br /> Love is love, magical or hormonal or both. Saying &amp;quot;blood bond is not real love&amp;quot; is purely a matter of putting up an ethical shield around a scary topic. </div> </div> </div> </div>That caveat is really important. Also, when I\u2019m in love I use a lot of \ud83d\udc97 emojis \ud83d\ude0a. (Mostly kidding, but still.)<br /> <br /> Everyone: this is a great discussion. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T15:58:46-07:00","id":1399153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399146#post1399146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel strongly that the idea that the bloodbond isn't &quot;real love&quot; to be wishful thinking. IDK, maybe I've never experienced true love because I've seen some depictions in media and, though I've looked at people and genuinely felt happy that they were happy, happy to be with them, and absolutely sure that I'd be very upset if something happened to them, and retroactively I thought my IQ dropped a hundred points, <i>My vision never went pink and flowers did not materialise in my vision. </i><br /> <br /> If the bloodbond does that to you, why isn't it love? I think you're looking at it from an ethical point of view, not a realistic point of view.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have a &quot;You absolutely want to fuck me power&quot; innate to them, and originally it only cared about target willpower and your good looks, but later on it got the caveat of &quot;but this power absolutely respects sexual orientation and doesn't work on people who don't like you&quot; and again, this is someone concerned about &quot;ethics&quot; rather than whats realistic (within a fantasy setting, yeah, nah, don't start that argument)<br /> <br /> Love is love, magical or hormonal or both. Saying &quot;blood bond is not real love&quot; is purely a matter of putting up an ethical shield around a scary topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Blood Bond isn't love, it's pathological obsession and devotion.<br /> <br /> The answer in simple terms is that the Blood Bond is not real life because it's mind-control. This isn't really a very hard concept to get. The Blood Bond makes you utterly and completely devoted to someone <i>regardless of how they treat you or actually feel about you</i>. The thing about real love is that you are capable of adapting to it. If your partner is an abusive awful jerk, you can get the hell out of there.<br /> <br /> With Kindred, you are stuck &quot;standing by your man&quot; or your woman no matter what because you are their slave. It is why most ghouls are 9 different kinds of fucked up. In addition to the fact the Blood is meth to the normal human, there's also the fact that most Kindred are abusive and dismissive to their slaves. So the ghouls try HARDER to impress their masters and this makes them MORE dismissive.<br /> <br /> With Kindred, it's the same thing and you are stuck with each other if you have a mutual Blood Bond. Everything that might irritate you about them is going to be replaced with a feeling of utter devotion even when you are STILL irritated by it. So it builds up until you have a double-consciousness about it. You hate them and you love them but you can't do anything about it because the blood controls your thoughts.<br /> <br /> The Paynes in the original Chicago by Night shows how this can become incredibly toxic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399148#post1399148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so you know, Desus got retconned out of 3e. Lillith's Solar mate in 3e was named Andamani.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they retcon the plot out? Because that's just weird. I mean, its meant to be horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T16:30:50-07:00","id":1399161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399153#post1399153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they retcon the plot out? Because that's just weird. I mean, its meant to be horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>3e Lilith's relationship to Andamani is very different from her relationship to 2e Desus. I think the previous writing kinda poisoned the well too much to continue using Desus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T17:20:35-07:00","id":1399168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399161#post1399161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e Lilith's relationship to Andamani is very different from her relationship to 2e Desus. I think the previous writing kinda poisoned the well too much to continue using Desus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I understand if he is something that impairs people's enjoyment factor. I just thought eventually Lilith would get to destroy his Death Lord in a suitably righteous fashion.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it may just be too &quot;horror movie&quot; for the whole thing. Presence and the Blood Bond make that kind of relationship very possible for vampires and it seems perfect for a Ghoul's relationship to their Regent. It's a very Black Dog and Hard-R thing that someone might not be looking for in their game about anime Bronze Age demigods.<br /> <br /> I can understand why 3E did away with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-26-2020, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T17:44:44-07:00","id":1399172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399150#post1399150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s scary. For real.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> what if one friend has over time developed something close to True Love for the guy and he definitely has feelings of True Love for her, but the other friend just really likes him?<br /> <br /> Of course, that\u2019s far afield from a mutual Blood Bond scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because my english skill failed so I have no idea who has now feelings to whom I just quoute W20. True Love is always mutual. If the target of True Love is another PC (s)he has to take True Love too because True Love can never be one sided. That is why differ between True Love and genuine love. True Love is this fairytale like setting where the couple loves each other the most of the world and so would do anything for eachother and do not care where they are as long they are together and where the love never ends because they always fell anew in love.<br /> And genuine Love where you honestly love someone from the bottom of your heart but you are as vampire somewhat selfish and so either keep her away from you despite both want rather to be together or/and you do what you think is the best for her/would make her happy but is not really what she really wish for.<br /> <br /> About that &quot;Is Love from blood bond real love?&quot; that is a complex theme which has for now no real objective answer because their is the hypothesis that all what we do is decided from our programming and we are all Biodroids. This fits in because like the human feeling of love is just a chemical cocktail too.<br /> My short answer to it is, it depends on the own decicion.<br /> The problem we have with blood bound is that it is an artificial created love feeling that we can have despite not wanting it. While it can happen, that we fell in love with the person we do not want to, I think here is the rather problem that it is much harder to just ignore it. So my opion is that blood bound can be genuine love if you decided to be bound on your own decision after it whas made you totally clear what the effect will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T17:45:09-07:00","id":1399173,"title":"","content":"Off-topic: I\u2019m glad they retconned Lilith. That relationship was really disturbing. A little more realism than I really want in an RPG, even from OPP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T17:46:00-07:00","id":1399174,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a> thank you for answering","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T17:52:37-07:00","id":1399175,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a> and I agree. Genuine love sometimes means one of you thinks it\u2019s best not to be together right now even though you both really want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T18:12:27-07:00","id":1399178,"title":"","content":"I think the big difference is the Blood Bond is basically being drugged versus freely given.<br /> <br /> You can choose to check in but like the Hotel California, can never leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T18:17:31-07:00","id":1399180,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> one more off topic: is that song about Cthulhu cultists?<br /> <br /> \u201cIn the Master\u2019s chambers<br /> They gathered for the feast<br /> Stabbed it with their steely knives<br /> But they just can\u2019t kill the Beast...\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T18:27:49-07:00","id":1399182,"title":"","content":"Mutual blood bonding makes sense as a strategy, in-world, in that it provides at least one vampire you can sort of trust, and prevents outside blood bonding. I mean, if you consider multiple mutual blood-bonds, this strategy seems to have worked for the Sabbat for roughly five hundred years. Arguably, it's the main reason the sect lasted as long as it has.<br /> <br /> The problem is, for the actual players playing the game around a table, having two vampires in a mutual bond leads to two characters who ignore everyone else and tend to retreat from plot interaction, rather than moving toward the plot.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Wait, your plan might lead to my beloved being endangered? Nope. We're out. We're going back to our haven to watch a Gilmore Girls marathon. Have fun storming the castle!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So, the game has set up a world with vampires who, for little reason, think of a mutual bond as a perversion.<br /> <br /> Forget the Golden Rule. The Platinum Rule is: &quot;That which moves pcs toward the action is good; that which leads them away is bad.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"u