ageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T18:44:05-07:00","id":1399186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399183#post1399183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually was inspired by that scene for a Sabbat dinner. The Tzimisce hosted a bound werewolf as the special cuisine.<br /> <br /> It ended badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice!!! When Will You Rage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T18:48:58-07:00","id":1399187,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11558_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11558\" data-vbnamecard=\"11558\">Nosimplehiway</a> very good point. Also applies when two of the players are too closely bonded and spend the whole night watching Outer Banks together on their phones and occasionally making out instead of actually gaming with the rest of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T19:07:27-07:00","id":1399190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1399018-is-mutual-blood-bonding-between-kindred-couples-a-good-thing-or-a-bad-thing?p=1399173#post1399173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off-topic: I\u2019m glad they retconned Lilith. That relationship was really disturbing. A little more realism than I really want in an RPG, even from OPP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that &quot;realism&quot; wasn't the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T19:22:38-07:00","id":1399192,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> I found it EXTREMELY disturbing. You think \u201crealism\u201d is the wrong word?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T19:24:55-07:00","id":1399193,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not gonna get triggered talking about it or anything. What made you think it wasn\u2019t realistic? And what do you think the problem was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T22:30:45-07:00","id":1399208,"title":"","content":"I mean it\u2019s a story and it feels like a story. And a clich\u00e9d story at that. <br /> <br /> The story of the woman who suffered abuse at the hands of a man - broken by him to the point that she barely does more than sleep in his absence - a woman who experiences a sudden awakening and lets the desire for a rampage of revenge consume her might be iconic, but it\u2019s <i>been done</i>, and you as a reader <i>deserve better</i>. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s sorta like how <i>Changeling: the Lost</i> is an allegory for surviving life after trauma, but a game of it needn\u2019t involve physically battling the Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-27-2020, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T23:49:43-07:00","id":1399221,"title":"","content":"It hit a lot of people much harder because while you're not going to ever see a guy leading an army of ghosts to exterminate a city so he can harvest their souls as citizens for his Necropolis built out of their bones, the idea of a guy who has the Charm of &quot;Beloved Celebrity&quot; using said status to gaslight a woman is an entirely different thing. The movie <i>Gaslight</i> is all about a woman's husband fucking with her sense of reality in hopes of keeping her under his control until he can get her committed (which was a real danger in the period).<br /> <br /> If it suits your game (and only IF--see Monty Cook's Consent supplement:<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/288535/Consent-in-Gaming\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...sent-in-Gaming</a> ) there's a lot to be harvested out of vampires using their powers as well as the Blood Bond in profoundly petty ways. Less &quot;take over the city&quot; and more, &quot;wield abosolute power over your loved ones.&quot;<br /> <br /> Blumehouse's THE INVISIBLE MAN remake is one of the most successful of them because it really did an excellent job of showing someone using a superpower to utterly terrify and abuse someone. It also backfired as quite a few audience members had horrifying pasts with abusive partners. It doesn't even have to be a partner as Desus could have used his &quot;Presence 5&quot; on, say, his children. The only JESSICA JONES season worth watching (I'm a Trish fan, can you tell?) is the first one. That is the perfect say to show what a Kindred can get up to with Dominate, albeit a bit OP and there probably ARE vampires who act entirely like that.<br /> <br /> We have abusive parents and the tricks they use to gaslight their children showing up in the SHE-RA remake now for instance.<br /> <br /> For those who like &quot;low stakes&quot; psychological horror, then there's plenty of inspiration to draw from--just don't make your players not have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T04:45:42-07:00","id":1399255,"title":"","content":"The story of Lilith and Desus bothered me for the exact opposite reason. It felt too real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T17:56:44-07:00","id":1403597,"title":"","content":"So I have reread the blood bonding part in V20 and I can now clarify a few things.<br /> First yes the love over the blood bond is real love, whas to be said as the closest possible to true love beside true love that exists but it is flawed ala something like the obsession of a Yandere.<br /> Then the feeling of Love in a Blood Bond is not consistent but changeing depending on how your binder treats you.<br /> If you are treated good and get regulary blood feeded, the bond will grow really strong like the person is the center of the universe.<br /> If misused, dismissive and only the needed dosis well then it is like a cheated Yandere. This brings me to next point.<br /> <br /> So yeah mutual blood bonding can turn out as something really good because part of it depends on how much respect you get and give and so in a function partnership let so bloom each the feeling of being in love and really loving the other person.<br /> The downside is, this is like another marriage there is conflict in the relationship you will ended bond to an enemy that is your Expartner.<br /> <br /> Though the risks comes with good stuff to like I said before that you can only be real bond to one person so as long there is no killing or Tremeremagic you will only end up with minor bondings that will get washed away by the feelings of the blood bond. Other thing is, you are as vampire not really feeling anything anymore so you know exactly when you found your true love because (s)he is not some strong liking or beautiful food but makes you really feel gaving the impression you never died.<br /> <br /> So mutual blood bonding outside of political marriages ie rare and can turn bad but if it happens it is for a couple to make them feel again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T18:07:54-07:00","id":1403601,"title":"","content":"Wow! A Yandere. I totally get it. (I have friends who love anime.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}